**Version**: 0.3
**Created**: 2026-07-10
**Status**: R1 OPERATIONAL — hardware-verified on the bare ESP32-C3 (2026-07-10). `firmware/reactive_core/`: a board-agnostic core (namespace store → bindings [bare-namespace OR `expr:` via the canonical `cyd/src/dsl`, compiled by-reference not forked] → publish-on-change sink, with a local write-back cascade depth-capped at 8) + a board seam (`board.h` + `boards/esp32c3_devkitm.cpp`, demo GPIO3 + on-board WS2812 mirror) + WiFi/MQTT app shell. Acceptance: `pio run -e esp32c3` clean (57.9% flash), host unit test 46/46 (incl. expr through the real DSL, publish-on-change suppression, dt/t parity, cascade, cycle-cap), no regressions (`native_dsl` 234/234). **Dispatcher hardware verify:** the **DSL corpus ran 234/234 on the C3 RISC-V soft-double** (219 µs/case) — the DSL is now bit-exact on TWO ESP32 arches (Xtensa 2b + RISC-V R1); and the reactive loop is LIVE — a Mac publish of `demo/level` drove the `ns('demo/level')>50` expr to GPIO3 (72→HIGH, 30→LOW, 88→HIGH) + the `clamp()` derived output, over real MQTT on 1883. **Decisions:** devices ride **:1883** (the shared ecosystem broker, not the 1884 foundation default — now the reactive_core platformio.ini default); demo GPIO3; the DSL needed ZERO changes for RISC-V. Seam flagged for a future [CXC-ER-CORE] change-record: the event-driven core's **local write-back cascade + depth-cap** (Python gets cycle-safety free from tick batching; an MCU event core needs the explicit cap).

**R2 OPERATIONAL — output-actuator HAL, HAL-logic hardware-verified on the C3 (2026-07-10).** `firmware/reactive_core/actuator_hal.{h,cpp}` — a declarative `ActuatorSpec` output HAL (peer consumer of bus arrivals AND core-derived outputs → "define once, actuate many"), three modes: **Binary** (dsl_truthy canon → GPIO+polarity), **PWM** (numeric scale in_min..in_max → 0..out_max duty, non-numeric withholds like the core), **Stepper** (Tier 2, value→target-position, a full-step sequencer paced on `tick(millis)`, `home_on_boot` no-feedback zeroing against the mechanical stop). Two board profiles behind the R1 seam: **lego_dots** (`light/1..12` → GPIO 0-10,20, BC337 low-side) + **rack_triple_gauge** (`gauge/1..3` steppers via MCP23017@0x20 → 3× L293D, I2C SDA4/SCL5; `gauge/N/light` PWM GPIO0/1/3). Acceptance: `pio run -e esp32c3|lego_dots|rack_triple_gauge` all clean, host test **94/94**, no regressions. Dispatcher verify on the bare C3: binary (light/1→GPIO4 HIGH/LOW), PWM (light/2=60→duty 153/255), stepper (gauge/1=50→120 steps→arrived) all correct from live MQTT. **STAGED FOR DAVID (boards not connected):** flash `-e lego_dots`/`-e rack_triple_gauge`, connect 12V + the board, watch the 12 lights / 3 needles (each output self-reports over serial). **Bring-up risk flagged:** lego_dots GPIO2/8/9 (CH3/9/10) are C3 strapping pins driving BC337 bases through only 150R — could clamp below VIL at reset (PCB concern; symptom = SuperMini boots bare but is dead seated in the board). rack_triple_gauge `out_max`=600 steps is a placeholder — tune to the real dial sweep. Seam-worthy for [CXC-HAL-ACTUATE]: `home_on_boot` zeroing + the on_value/tick command split.

**R3 OPERATIONAL — CYD reactive display, hardware-verified (2026-07-10).** The R1 core compiled **BY REFERENCE** into the CYD Xtensa firmware (`cyd/src/reactive_core_canonical.cpp` includes `reactive_core.cpp`, byte-untouched) — **[CXC-ER-BOARDS] "one core, three variants" now proven (C3 + actuator boards + CYD)**. Added: an esp-mqtt bus client (`bus_mqtt.cpp`, :1883, BusMessage parity, buttons now publish for real); on-device `.compose.yaml` binding parse (`reactive_apply.h` + `compose_scene`: bare-ns / object-form / `expr:` via the on-chip DSL / widget-level `namespace:`; `map/when/invert` honestly refused); **widget-level dirty-band repaint** (`canvas render_bands`); event-driven static-scene rendering (bus arrival → dirty bands only; tap → full; idle → nothing — replaces M5's unconditional loop); and an **on-device pull capture server** (`GET /capture.bmp` renders a fresh frame — the reactive-verify hook). Main-task stack raised to 24 KB for on-chip DSL parse. Acceptance: `pio run -e cyd` clean; **R1 core byte-untouched + R1 `native_test` 128 checks + `esp32c3` + R2 boards all still build**; no regressions (`cyd_dsl_test`/`native_dsl` 234/234). **Dispatcher hardware-verify (capture-server framebuffer diff, no eyes):** publish `demo/gauge=72` → 2.4% pixels changed (needle + value text); `=90 + demo/alert=on` → 18.8% (`ns('demo/gauge')>75` LED + red ALERT banner appear); **dup `90` → 0.00% (publish-on-change: zero repaint)** — the DSL expr, binding→attr, dirty-band, and suppression all confirmed against real pixels. Decisions: pull capture server (not push — reactive verify needs "publish→GET frame"; sidesteps M5's single-client wedge; BMP not PNG, no on-chip encoder); `map/when/invert` refused (silent-intent-inversion worse than none). Seam for [CXC-ER-RENDER]: the render lock (capture vs render task vs touch SPI) is the CYD's concurrency contract; the 24 KB main-task stack for on-device DSL should be recorded against [CXC-DSL]'s scene-task budget.

**R4 OPERATIONAL — reactive core on the ESP32-S3, hardware-verified (2026-07-10).** A clean PORT (Opus): the R1 core compiled BY REFERENCE onto the Adafruit Qualia **ESP32-S3 (Xtensa LX7)**, headless (only a new `firmware/reactive_core/src/boards/qualia_s3.cpp` — demo GPIO17, no actuators, no display). `[env:qualia_s3]` (board `esp32-s3-devkitc-1`, native-USB CDC console, PSRAM enabled-not-load-bearing) + `[env:qualia_s3_dsl_test]` (the 2b harness + corpus reused verbatim; `sdkconfig.s3.defaults` USB-Serial-JTAG console; the existing `IDF_TARGET != esp32` CMake branch builds dsl+harness for esp32s3). Acceptance: both build clean; **R1 core byte-untouched (git diff empty)**; `esp32c3`/`cyd`/`native_test` 128/`native_dsl` 234/234 all still pass. **Dispatcher hardware-verify: DSL corpus 234/234 on the Qualia S3 LX7** (197 µs/case) — the DSL is now bit-exact on **all three ESP32 arches: LX6 (classic/CYD, 2b) + RISC-V (C3, R1) + LX7 (S3, R4)**. The DSL needed ZERO changes for the S3. [CXC-ER-BOARDS] "one core, three variants" fully proven. (S3 flash needed one upload retry — a transient native-USB re-enumeration, then verified.)

R5 next (Qualia RGB666 display — the one genuinely hard slice: parallel panel + framebuffer + live transforms). Foundation: `firmware/esp32_mqtt_client/` + `cyd/src/dsl`.

**§5 DRADIS contacts widget ADDED to spec (2026-07-16, design-intent — NOT yet hardware-verified).** Encoded the `dradis_contacts` reactive radar-contact widget as a capability under [CXC-EMBED-REACTIVE] ([CXC-ER-DRADIS] + BUS/PROJ/MOTION/BLINK/HUD), a worked example of state-on-bus/behavior-in-widget on a display widget destined for the R5 Qualia surface. Normative source: `docs/dradis/contacts-contract.md`. Three design decisions carry `change`/`context_for_change` blocks (all 2026-07-16): **D1** `range` → physical light-seconds on a log scope (on [CXC-ER-DRADIS-BUS]); **D2** contact heading derived at the display leaf, not bussed (on [CXC-ER-DRADIS-MOTION], the corpus's decentralization exemplar); **D3** ping-on-sweep-pass REMOVED (on [CXC-ER-DRADIS]). The motion indicator is linked EXEMPLIFIES [DP-CIO-3] + [CXC-BIND-PRINCIPLE]. **Architect: two ratifications flagged — (1) new domain relationship verb `EXEMPLIFIES` (fallback: existing `UPHOLDS`); (2) whether D1/D2/D3 should also spawn companion DELTA docs per SPEC §8, or whether the in-node `change` blocks suffice as this domain has done for prior in-place decisions (e.g. [CXC-BIND] canon change).**

**§5 DRADIS game-layer RENDERING facts ADDED (2026-07-16, second pass, design-intent — NOT hardware-verified).** Extended §5 with the RENDERING-tier half of the game layer (the GAME/sensor-model half lives in a separate app-layer spec, which DEPENDS_ON this platform spec — the correct dependency direction): **[CXC-ER-DRADIS-BODIES]** (the `dradis/bodies` stellar backdrop — star/planet/asteroid rendered UNDER contacts through the same log projection, no blink/motion/tally; staged stellar assets; two OPEN items recorded as caveats — no dedicated star art yet, and the ~490 KB 350×350 BMP32 stellar assets exceed the 160 KB on-device fetch buffer → Qualia buffer bump or smaller asset, a build-time item); **[CXC-ER-DRADIS-IDENT]** (fog-of-war renders with ZERO display change — the publisher republishes the same `id` with an evolved `type`/`allegiance` so the icon morphs in place; framed as the THIRD decentralization exemplar in this widget, but the OPPOSITE case from heading — identification is engine-held ground truth, published not derived). Also: a `sensed-classification` note + the full staged icon registry added to [CXC-ER-DRADIS-BUS] `type`; compliance rows CXC-ER-C13/C14; relationships for the two new nodes (BODIES USES [CXC-ER-DRADIS-PROJ]; IDENT EXEMPLIFIES [DP-CIO-3] + [CXC-BIND-PRINCIPLE]). Normative source: `docs/dradis/contacts-contract.md` "# Game layer (added 2026-07-16)".

**§6 Remote Config-Reload (bus restart command) ADDED to spec (2026-07-30, design-intent — NOT yet built).** Encoded the SPEC leg of the record→spec→implement directive for [DEC-ESP32-REMOTE-RESTART-BUS-COMMAND] (`corpora/intelligence-console/decision-graph-composeux-architect.lts`, David's ruling 2026-07-30 — a fundamental platform decision; born from the 2026-07-30 dradis deploy where an updated engine-controls config PUT to bus_storage could not reach the Qualia `(a device id, not published)` without a power cycle). Two new nodes under [SPEC:CXC-EMBED-REACTIVE]: **[CXC-ER-REMOTE-RESTART]** (every ESP32-class device honors a remote-restart command → hard `esp_restart()` → re-runs the EXISTING boot-fetch → loads the updated YAML; MVP = hard restart; lives in the shared firmware app shell so ALL envs inherit it) and **[CXC-ER-RESTART-BUS]** (the bus contract). **Namespace + payload firmed:** BOTH a per-device `_device/<id>/restart` (`<id>` = the config id keying `bus://assets/displays/<id>.compose.yaml`) AND a broadcast `_device/restart` are honored; payload = truthy (`dsl_truthy` canon; canonical `{"restart": true}`, any truthy form accepted; falsy/empty = NO-OP). **Judgment calls recorded:** (1) **ACK convention recommended** — pre-restart `_device/<id>/status` = "restarting" + the existing post-boot `_bus/discovery/<id>` announce close the loop (a silent restart is invisible); (2) **broadcast-vs-per-device precedence** — equivalent triggers, no conflict; the boot-guard window makes a double-fire idempotent (restart once); (3) **retained/boot-loop guard** — command MUST be non-retained + firmware ignores restart within the boot window (a retained truthy would loop the fleet). **Scope boundary stated (load-bearing):** CONFIG-reload NOT firmware-OTA — a new firmware capability still needs a USB flash / a future separate ESP32-OTA capability. **Control-plane legitimacy noted:** the device is the CONSUMER of its own control namespace, NOT the [CXC-PS-SEMANTIC-OWNERSHIP] anti-pattern. Soft in-place reload (no reboot; `yaml_min.h` already frees on reload) recorded as a future variant, out of MVP scope. Compliance C15–C19; relationships for the two nodes. Realizes the `config/reload` follow-on on [DEC-FETCH-ON-BOOT-CONFIG-DISCIPLINE]. **Architect: two ratifications flagged — (1) whether the ACK convention (`_device/<id>/status` "restarting" + boot-counter in the presence announce) is mandated (SHOULD → MUST) or left recommended; (2) whether this capability warrants its own follow-on OTA spec node now or when the OTA decision is taken.** IMPLEMENT leg next: shared ESP32 firmware, all envs.

**Spec 29 decoupled from the app — now platform-independent (2026-07-17).** In the platform/app refactor the game/sensor-model half was relocated to the bsg app spec (`bsg spec/10-dradis-game.lts`), which DEPENDS-ON this platform spec (the correct direction — the app depends on the platform, never the reverse). Removed the two backward app-coupling relationship edges ([CXC-ER-DRADIS-IDENT] RELATED_TO the game spec; and [SPEC:CXC-EMBED-REACTIVE] RENDERS-FOR the game spec — the sole use of the freeform `RENDERS-FOR` verb, now retired) and softened the three prose refs (the [CXC-ER-DRADIS-BUS] `sensed-classification` note, the [CXC-ER-DRADIS-IDENT] key-insight, and the changelog above) to describe the GENERAL capability: the `dradis_contacts` widget renders a namespace-driven contact scope; the publishing APPLICATION owns the sensor/identification model (an app-layer concern). Identification remains published state the display consumes as `type`/`allegiance` (the display cannot recompute true type from range) — the decentralization/exemplar insight is intact; the game spec is simply no longer named. The platform widget capability ([CXC-ER-DRADIS*] nodes) is unchanged.

**[CXC-ER-DEVICE] + [CXC-ER-REMOTE-RESTART] now realized on the OUTPUT/ACTUATOR tier — the first HEADLESS ACTUATOR devices (2026-08-05, hardware-verified).** The config-fetch-on-boot device model ([CXC-ER-DEVICE]) and the remote config-reload path ([CXC-ER-REMOTE-RESTART], `_device/<id>/restart`) were previously proven only by DISPLAY-tier devices (CYD/Qualia). `office_fan` + `office_hepa` — generic ESP32-WROOM-32E integrated 4-relay boards running `reactive_core` unchanged — now prove BOTH on the headless output/actuator tier: each GETs its `.compose.yaml` at boot and self-configures a break-before-make relay bank (no baked pins), and honors a live re-fetch via `_device/<id>/restart` with no power-cycle. The descriptor + the break-before-make invariant live in the peripheral-HAL spec as **[CXC-HAL-RELAY-ACTUATOR]** (Output Tier-1, spec 27, hardware-verified same session) — NOT duplicated here; this note records only the realization on the [CXC-ER-*] config-fetch / remote-reload path.
